			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I love this stuff though. For my OpenAPI client (it's own typescript monstrosity, for the record), I plan to fully type the output URL of .compile to be exactly what it is fetching in the code (ie: /route/page?limit=10 *is* the type). Just for fun.</p><p>It's annoying how typescript really likes to throw fully typed strings into the void whenever you aren't careful (ie `(\"1\" | \"2\") + (\"1\" | \"2\") -&gt; string` instead of `\"12\" | \"11\" | \"21\" | \"22\"`</p><p><a href=\"https://github.com/boehs/ajar\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"\">github.com/boehs/ajar</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a></p>",
